---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ShipGlows | Business-aware delivery"
  description="Why ShipGlows acts as a business-aware delivery partner, who it serves, and how its métiers carry work through proof."
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <NavBar />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">About ShipGlows</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">AI agents need more than instructions. They need a governed understanding of what the product is trying to achieve.</h1>
        <p>
          ShipGlows exists because technically competent work can still be the
          wrong work. Product intent gets lost, business context becomes stale,
          agents optimize locally, and a polished answer is mistaken for an
          owned result.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <article class="price-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who It Is For</p>
          <h2>Solo founders first, with a real fit for small product teams</h2>
          <p>
            ShipGlows is for people shipping real products with agents who want
            leverage without becoming the full-time coordinator of prompts,
            files, specialists, checks, and releases.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="price-card accent-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">What It Solves</p>
          <h2>The gap between business intent and technically finished work</h2>
          <p>
            The product connects governed truth, useful judgment, accountable
            métier ownership, bounded execution, and visible proof so a chantier
            stays attached to the outcome that justified it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What It Is</p>
        <h2>A business-aware delivery partner built as a system of accountable métiers.</h2>
        <p>
          ShipGlows can question weak framing, compare credible directions, and
          recommend a professional default. Once a direction is approved, the
          responsible métier carries it through execution and proof. Governance,
          environments, server operations, and release controls support that
          promise instead of competing with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="doc-grid">
        {[
          ["Not a passive executor", "ShipGlows does not treat every request as a technical ticket. When business truth changes the right move, it loads that truth, exposes the consequence, and keeps the operator’s authority visible."],
          ["Not an oracle", "ShipGlows can recommend and challenge, but it does not claim infallible advice or guarantee launch, growth, revenue, conversion, security, or defect-free delivery."],
          ["Not another prompt library", "The product combines governed context, métier ownership, approval boundaries, verification, and durable handoffs. Prompt wording alone is not the operating model."],
          ["Not a server product first", "Environment and runtime capabilities remain useful delivery infrastructure. They are supporting evidence and operational leverage, not the leading customer promise."],
          ["Why the contracts matter", "Business, product, GTM, brand, architecture, and quality contracts give each kind of truth one owner so agents can detect drift instead of inventing a second strategy."],
          ["Why the métiers matter", "Thirteen public métiers give creation, quality, publishing, growth, governance, and organization clear ownership while the internal lifecycle stays out of the operator’s way."]
        ].map(([title, body]) => (
          <article class="doc-card">
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Start With The Outcome</p>
        <h2>Bring ShipGlows the result you want—not the workflow you think you need.</h2>
        <p>
          Explore the métiers, inspect the governing contracts, and challenge
          the public promise before deciding whether this partnership fits the
          way you want to build.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/skills">Explore the métiers</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs">Inspect the contracts</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/faq">Read the boundaries</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/blog/shipglows-and-t3-code-same-conviction-different-scope">
            Our relationship to T3 Code
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
